<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Kadesh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1258 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a> · Also known as Egyptian–Hittite peace treaty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a>, also known as the Egyptian–Hittite peace treaty, was concluded in 1258 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-iii">Hattusili III</a>. It followed years of rivalry after the Battle of Kadesh and established peace, mutual defence and the return of fugitives. Copies survive in both Egyptian and Hittite versions, and it is often described as the earliest known peace treaty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kadesh.jpg" alt="Treaty of Kadesh" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olaf Tausch · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karnak_%C3%84gyptisch-Hethitischer_Friedensvertrag_06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
